    "result": "Perfect! The bug is fixed. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was caused by the `frai` CLI's Commander.js configuration not properly passing the `--ci` flag through to the `frai-gate` subcommand. When running `frai gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag was being consumed by the main program level and never reaching the gate subcommand.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**File: `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`**\n\n1. **Added `enablePositionalOptions(true)` to the main program** (line 604):\n   - This tells Commander to allow positional options in subcommands\n\n2. **Added `passThroughOptions(true)` to the gate command** (line 742):\n   - This tells Commander to pass known options (like `--ci`) through to the subcommand instead of consuming them at the main level\n\n## Verification\n\n\u2705 The fix has been tested and verified:\n- Running `frai gate init --ci` now correctly:\n  - Creates `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n  - Creates `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` (the GitHub Actions workflow)\n  \nBoth files are now being generated as expected.",
